readme.text:
**This is the reason you can install the plugin and stop patching files.**

On a stock `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-rc.2` install the main-path conversation request is deep-frozen by the host *before* it reaches `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm`. Its entry point is:

```js
stream(options) { return this.streamWithRegistration(options) }
streamWithRegistration(options, prepared) {
  return this.ctx.waterfall(this, "llm/stream", options, () => this.adapterStream(options, prepared))
}

* request is **frozen** → shallow copy + `messages` array copy + every message object copied, then re-marked through `markAgentLoopRequest` taken from the host's own `dsh-llm` module, and the copy enters `llm/stream`;
* request is **not frozen** (host already patched) → passed through untouched, byte for byte. Zero behaviour change;
* anything unexpected → logged and passed through untouched. This plugin never turns a working session into a broken one.

1. derives candidate locations from `process.argv` (the real `…/@deepseek-ai/dsh/lib/bin.js` — on the desktop shell it sits in `argv[2]`, not `argv[1]`), from `createRequire` resolution of the host entry, and from `$DSH_HOME/profiles{/*}/node_modules`;
2. imports each candidate and **round-trip tests** it against the actual request: the first copy whose `isAgentLoopRequest(options)` returns `true` is the host's own instance and is used;
3. if none matches, it warns once and takes over anyway with the first copy. **Honest limitation:** in that case context rewriting still works, but `@deepseek-ai/dsh-session-title` may stop auto-titling sessions, because it checks the same `WeakSet`. This has been observed on one npm-style install layout and not on the desktop layout. Nothing else in DSH consumes that marker.

- **Which patches**: each row gives the patch id, the package and file it edits, and why this plugin wants it (marked *required* or *recommended*);
- **How to apply them (any one of three)**: **A** press "Copy the prompt" and hand the whole block to **your own agent** (it runs a read-only health check first, applies one patch at a time, and stops to ask you if a hunk does not match); **B** use the patch library script, `node apply.mjs --check` then `node apply.mjs --apply --only <id>`; **C** apply by hand, `cd <package> && git apply -p1 <library>/patches/<id>/change.diff`;
- **The patch library**: <https://github.com/xiamubumu/dsh-patch-library> (ten self-contained patches, an adaptive applier, five ways to apply them);
- **Detection**: judged from the `*.orig` backup next to each target file plus a **content hash** against the library manifest (`pristine` / `patched`). When neither can decide, it says **"cannot tell"** outright and never guesses "applied";
- **Once applied, it stops appearing.** The dialog offers "Later" (this once) and "Do not remind me again" (permanent, recorded **per patch id** — a patch added later still gets announced).

1. The other plugin **rebuilds** the same seam wholesale (rewrites the whole system prompt / tool result) instead of editing incrementally;
2. The other plugin takes the **same `chain`** slot (this plugin takes no slot at all, so only the other side is affected);
3. Both need a patch to the **same official file** — reported as an explicit `conflict` by the patch library `apply.mjs --check`, never as a silent failure.

**这一段就是「装完插件就不必再改文件」的原因。**

原版 `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-rc.2` 里，主线路的对话请求在进入 `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` 之前就已经被宿主**深度冻结**。它的入口长这样：

```js
stream(options) { return this.streamWithRegistration(options) }
streamWithRegistration(options, prepared) {
  return this.ctx.waterfall(this, "llm/stream", options, () => this.adapterStream(options, prepared))
}
